elow, these proteins are present in all of the above-mentioned species. Of these proteins, the following are homologous to each other: PG0179, PG2133; PG0217, PG0218; PG0816, PG1458; PG0831, PG1442; PG2130, PG2168.</p><p><sup>+</sup>Not found at present in either 1 or both <italic>Prevotella </italic>species.</p><p><sup>x</sup>Missing in one of the <italic>Bacteroides </italic>species as well as <italic>Prevotella </italic>species.</p><p><sup>#</sup>Also present was <italic>C. phaeobacteroides </italic>BS1.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T5"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>Proteins that are Specific for Species from the Flavobacteriales Order</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="center"><bold>orf No. [Accession No.]</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Possible/Predicted Function</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Genome ID No. [Accession No.]</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Possible/Predicted Function</bold></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">orf89 [<ext-link ext-link-type="gen" xlink:href="CAL65078">CAL65078</ext-link>]<sup>b</sup></td><td align="left">membrane protein</td><td align="left">orf1826 [<ext-link ext-link-type="gen" xlink:href="CAL66812">CAL66812</ext-link>]</td><td align="left">hypothetical protein</td></tr><tr><td align="left">orf92 [<ext-link ext-link-type="gen" xlink:href="CAL65081">CAL65081</ext-link>]</td><td align="left">secreted protein</td><td align="left">orf1872 [<ext-link ext-link-type="gen" xlink:href="CAL66858">CAL66858</ext-link>]</td><td align="left">hypothetical protein</td></tr><tr><td align="left">orf107 [<ext-link ext-link-type="gen" xlink:href="CAL65096">CAL65096</ext-link>]</td><td align="left">membrane protein</td><td align="left">orf2280 [<ext-link ext-link-type="gen" xlink:href="CAL67264">CAL67264</ext-link>]<sup>c</sup></td><td align="left">hypothetical protein</td></tr><tr><td align="left">orf110 [<ext-link ext-link-type="gen" xlink:href="C